    {
      "field_name": "diagnostic_criteria",
      "value": "Clinical features (stiffness, spasms, hyperlordosis); EMG showing continuous motor unit activity; Anti GAD antibodies were negative; MRI of the spine was normal; Nerve conduction studies were normal",
      "quote": "On examination, she had hyper lumbar lordosis with rock hard lumbar paraspinal muscles and deep lumbar furrowing [Figure 1]. Both legs were stiff (left more than right) and there was clawing of the left toes [Ashworth scale 5]. Motor and sensory examination was normal. Her gait was slow, cautious and 'tin soldier' like. Anti GAD antibodies were negative and MRI of the spine was normal. Nerve conduction studies were normal. EMG studies showed continuous motor unit activity from the lumbar paraspinal muscles. A paraneoplastic work up was negative. She was diagnosed as SMS variant of SPS.",
      "confidence": "high"
    },
